[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-136824"] :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}^{2}\\ge -3{x}_{1}^{2},\\,-{x}_{3}^{2}\\ge -3{x}_{3}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge -3{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =-3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=-3(1)=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge -3.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $-3.$ But before we conclude that $-3$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=-3.$\n\nNotice that when $x={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2(0)^{2}-3(1)^{2}-(0)^{2} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-136826"] :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=7{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{2}^{2}+5{x}_{3}^{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )((8-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +36) & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,7,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-138021/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "cf9bbfe3-7cda-58d8-9e59-d2b23e980625" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138021/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "af575672-518e-5c18-97a4-7800770c87bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138021/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "570fa96e-3f08-52ec-a22c-f6cbf778bccb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138021/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "783b1f87-c0c1-52ab-b346-f4b0e7ffa15c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138021/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "403c9b07-0dbf-5f77-9560-97c8f7accf6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138021/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a1a0e64-0272-581c-b947-b7159d4ba4d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-138021/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-138021/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-138021/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-138021/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-138021/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-138021/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138021" :question/id #uuid "e597502b-9616-570d-85d2-53bc922c89a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-138021" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n-4{x}_{2}^{2}\\le 2{x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result,  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=2(1)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\le 2.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $2.$ But before we conclude that $2$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=2.$\n\nNotice that when $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(1)^{2}-4(0)^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-138021/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8666dd9-b763-589d-8ae3-af203068f1a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138021"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-138075/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "96a49ce8-3f28-5914-84bf-3b936394fe87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138075/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "72fa2eec-6654-534c-a590-986e55e83815" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138075/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "436bda34-cb0d-5656-bab6-32c9314c9e95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138075/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "afa5ab4c-d59f-5f0f-b646-b00c93517035" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138075/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "6ef97c89-1186-547d-b913-95f149ca450b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138075/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "181f6ac5-2654-51a3-9fe9-66b5cd5682ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-138075/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-138075/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-138075/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-138075/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-138075/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-138075/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138075" :question/id #uuid "f07b8c52-650b-58ad-8dad-c02bf167a0ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-138075" :question/problem "Find the  maximum value of $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -3) & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =3,\\,2,\\,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}=3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-138075/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b2e9ac0-590b-587c-b16d-309f899c21e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138075"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-158533/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "7d8be8fd-4e39-54e9-b47b-0d3aa3dc7cf1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158533/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "3bb6a164-f073-5ef0-9012-24ee58aa1fc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158533/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "a4a8027a-b384-551a-9e90-c6f1eb741c9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158533/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "b50f7c23-2861-5c61-9b1a-75dc826db19f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158533/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "63be96b9-041a-53cd-aecf-b20ee1f44375" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158533/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b937ceeb-0702-54ca-b035-2404b89bb3d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-158533/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-158533/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-158533/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-158533/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-158533/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-158533/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-158533" :question/id #uuid "ab8bdada-0761-5c9a-8f04-e9214224aca7" :question/math-academy-id "q-158533" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n6{x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 3{x}_{2}^{2},\\,4{x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 3{x}_{3}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge 3{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=3(1)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge 3.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $3.$ But before we conclude that $3$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=3.$\n\nNotice that when  $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =3(1)^{2}+6(0)^{2}+4(0)^{2} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-158533/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f7fa4d-9ac0-552a-9f3e-9e09c2ed0286"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158533"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
